# Everything about the people this gets built for stays out of this (public) repo:
# their name, greeting, playlist, photo, song list, generated deck and PDFs. Each
# people/<slug>/ is meant to be its own *private* repo cloned in here (see README.md
# "Adding a person"); the only thing tracked is the template. Without any
# people/<slug>/ the build falls back to a single generic "Musikster" flavor.
/people/*
!/people/person.example.json
# Pre-restructure output location; PDFs now land in people/<slug>/print/.
/deck_output/

# Loose working photos/exports for the scripts/*.py coin & plaque pipeline —
# inputs/outputs of a one-off physical-gift run, not source. Point the scripts'
# CLI args at your own photo to reuse them.
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png
/*.svg
/*.docx
/pictures/

# Release signing keystore — private key material, never commit. GitHub Actions
# gets its own copy via the KEYSTORE_BASE64/KEYSTORE_PASSWORD/KEY_ALIAS/KEY_PASSWORD
# repo secrets instead (see .github/workflows/build.yml).
*.jks
*-credentials.txt
